"The diagram illustrates the design of a contemporary landfill for domestic waste and how it works.": "",
"Overall, the process can be divided into four stages, beginning with the excavation of the ground and ending with the sealing of the landfill and the management of gases produced by the decomposing waste.": "",
"At the first stage of the process, to create storage for household waste, people manually excavate the ground until an artificial crater is formed above the natural rock layer.": "",
"Next, the interior sides of this hole are lined with a layer of synthetic material, over which a layer of clay is applied to prevent leakage.": "",
"At the bottom of the hole, organic matter — including layers of newspaper, grass (each approximately 15 cm deep), and food waste — is placed, and a system of drainage pipes is installed above a drainage tank to collect leachate from the waste.": "",
"At the subsequent stage, trucks transport household waste to the landfill and release it directly into the pit.": "",
"Liquid from the waste trickles down through the organic layers and is collected in the drainage tank below.": "",
"After the pit has been filled to capacity, it is completely sealed using a clay cap on top.": "",
"Finally, a system of pipes is installed to channel the gases produced by the decomposing waste out of the sealed landfill, completing the process.": "",
